  "meta": {
    "status": "live",
    "notes": "A separate one-pass street-diamond prototype. Approach northwest on Olympia Way: turn down 20th Avenue and Washington Way for the shorter main path, or continue on Olympia and sweep down Kessler Boulevard on the longer outer alternate. Both reconnect at Washington before its mapped bridge and the shared 30th Avenue finish. Source OSM captured 2026-10-15; USGS 3DEP source elevation. Arcade lane widths, grass margins, eased corners and junction movements are adaptations, not surveyed lanes, verified turn restrictions or current access advice. Generic town scenery is not mapped properties. Lake Sacajawea and nearby unnamed water polygons use preserved source geometry with separate approximate DEM-median levels; four mapped lake holes remain dry. Bounded source terrain replaces legacy town scatter; only explicit physical frontage scenes remain. Site grades support those scenes. Shoreline precision, clipped outer coverage and elevation limits are recorded in the terrain manifest. No nested Hudson choice, reward compensation or claim of time parity."
  }
